{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"operations\":[{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-return-trigger-link\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-16\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Assessing whether return or destruction is required upon termination of the agreement.\",\"inspection\":\"Identify both the required act and its triggering event. A duty triggered only by the discloser's request does not establish a termination-triggered duty; termination, expiration, rejection, conclusion, or abandonment must itself activate the duty.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the operative return-or-destruction duty together with language linking it to termination or an equivalent end event.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,88,331,238,245],\"rationale\":\"Cases 334 and 88 show the recurring request-versus-termination error, while 331, 238, and 245 establish that conclusion or termination language supplies the required trigger.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-post-return-retention-permission\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-20\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement contains an exception to a return or destruction obligation.\",\"inspection\":\"Check whether the exception expressly permits continued possession of backups, archival material, a legal copy, or another defined subset after the return/destruction event. Conditions on access, purpose, or continuing confidentiality do not negate the permission.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the retention exception and, when separated, the governing return/destruction clause showing the temporal context.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,245],\"rationale\":\"Cases 334 and 245 show that narrow archival or legal-retention exceptions establish post-event possession even though retained material remains restricted.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-exhaustive-return-bars-retention\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-20\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement requires return or destruction of confidential information and copies without stating a retention exception.\",\"inspection\":\"Determine whether the duty is exhaustive as to the covered material and copies. A complete return/destruction command that leaves no authorized retained subset negates permission to possess some material afterward.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Contradiction\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the exhaustive operative duty and verify across the complete agreement that no backup, archival, legal-copy, or other retention exception qualifies it.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,88,331,238,245],\"rationale\":\"Cases 490, 88, 331, and 238 contrast exhaustive return duties with the express exceptions in 245; the absence of an exception must be checked globally rather than inferred from one fragment.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-no-rights-grant\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-15\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement addresses ownership, licenses, or rights in confidential information or associated intellectual property.\",\"inspection\":\"Look for language that no license or right is granted, conveyed, conferred, or implied. A limited authorization to review or use information for the stated transaction does not by itself contradict the broader no-grant proposition.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the express no-grant clause; include an ownership clause only when it helps establish the object of the denied rights.\",\"source_operations\":[]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,88,331,238,245],\"rationale\":\"All six witnesses label express no-license or no-rights language as entailment; case 238 exposes the polarity error of treating limited permitted use as a contrary grant.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-negotiation-existence-secrecy\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-10\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement restricts disclosure of negotiations, discussions, a contemplated transaction, or the existence of dealings between the parties.\",\"inspection\":\"Treat a prohibition on revealing that negotiations or discussions are occurring as covering the fact of the agreement or negotiation, even when the restriction is framed as disclosure to the public or media rather than as secrecy of the document itself.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the prohibition and the text identifying the protected fact; retain any governing introduction needed to show that the listed fact is prohibited from disclosure.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,88],\"rationale\":\"Cases 334 and 88 show two formulations of the same protected fact; case 88 demonstrates that a public-media limitation is still an express nondisclosure rule.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-universal-identification-condition\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-1\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Confidential-information coverage is conditioned on marking, designation, or identification by the disclosing party.\",\"inspection\":\"Confirm that every covered disclosure mode is subject to an express identification mechanism, including any oral or non-written mode. A universal marking rule may use different procedures for written and oral disclosures.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite all clauses needed to cover each disclosure mode and its identification requirement; do not rely on one mode while another remains unconditional.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,331],\"rationale\":\"Cases 490 and 331 support entailment where the definition or paired procedures condition the full covered universe on identification.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-contextual-confidentiality-alternative\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-1\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The definition covers information either expressly designated confidential or reasonably understood to be confidential from its nature or disclosure circumstances.\",\"inspection\":\"The contextual alternative independently covers undesignated information, so express identification by the disclosing party is not required for all confidential information.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Contradiction\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the complete alternative definition showing both designation and circumstance- or nature-based coverage.\",\"source_operations\":[]}},\"source_case_ids\":[88],\"rationale\":\"Case 88 supplies the separating condition: contextual knowledge is an alternative to designation and therefore contradicts a universal express-identification requirement.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-copy-permission-explicit\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-17\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Assessing whether the receiving party may make any copy in some circumstance.\",\"inspection\":\"Find an express copying route, such as prior written consent, copies needed for authorized persons, or automatic backup creation acknowledged by the agreement. Permission may be conditional and need not be general.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite language expressly addressing copying, reproduction, or backup creation and the condition that authorizes it; access or disclosure permission alone is insufficient.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[334,88,331,238,245],\"rationale\":\"Cases 334 and 245 establish genuine conditional copying routes, while 88, 331, and 238 show that employee access or general protective measures must not be converted into copy permission.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-unqualified-copy-ban\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-17\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement expressly prohibits copying confidential information.\",\"inspection\":\"If copying is barred and the complete agreement provides no condition under which the receiving party may copy, the conditional-copy permission hypothesis is negated. A consent exception would instead be a permission circumstance.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Contradiction\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the copy prohibition and verify that no consent, operational-copy, backup, or other copying exception appears elsewhere.\",\"source_operations\":[]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,245],\"rationale\":\"Case 490 demonstrates contradiction from a copy ban, while 334 and 245 prevent overbroad application because their clauses supply consent-based or purpose-based exceptions.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-third-party-representative-sharing\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-7\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement permits disclosure to representatives or other persons.\",\"inspection\":\"Resolve who falls within the permitted class. Consultants, agents, counsel, accountants, professional advisers, affiliates, and similar non-employees establish sharing with some third parties; an employee-only exception does not.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite both the permission and the definition or enumeration proving that at least one permitted recipient is a third party, plus any need-to-know or confidentiality condition governing the permission.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,238,245],\"rationale\":\"Cases 334, 238, and 245 contain qualifying non-employee recipients, whereas 490 permits only employees and therefore supplies the necessary limiting contrast.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-purpose-limited-use\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-4\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"The agreement states an authorized transaction, project, evaluation, business relationship, or other defined purpose for confidential information.\",\"inspection\":\"A command to use confidential information only for that purpose, or not for any other purpose, directly imposes the limited-use obligation. The existence of the authorized purpose is not a contradiction.\",\"relation_if_established\":\"Entailment\",\"evidence_requirement\":\"Cite the operative use restriction and enough purpose language to identify the authorized scope.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,88,331,238,245],\"rationale\":\"All six witnesses treat purpose-only use language as entailment; case 88 exposes the mistaken polarity that interpreted an express limitation as contradiction.\"},{\"operation\":\"CREATE\",\"target_ids\":[],\"skill\":{\"id\":\"nda-list-and-fragment-completeness\",\"hypothesis_ids\":[\"nda-2\",\"nda-3\",\"nda-5\",\"nda-7\",\"nda-8\",\"nda-12\",\"nda-13\",\"nda-16\",\"nda-20\"],\"guidance\":{\"when\":\"Relevant candidate text is a numbered item, exception, continuation, anaphoric clause, or otherwise incomplete fragment.\",\"inspection\":\"Read the governing introduction and adjacent items to determine the item's legal function, trigger, subject, and exceptions. Keep independent operative clauses separately; do not treat a neighboring item as evidence merely because it shares the list.\",\"relation_if_established\":null,\"evidence_requirement\":\"Include every span necessary to make the relied-on proposition complete, while excluding sibling items that do not establish that proposition.\",\"source_operations\":[\"list_preamble\"]}},\"source_case_ids\":[490,334,88,331,238,245],\"rationale\":\"Across all six witnesses, many correct labels had missing list introductions or governing clauses, while several answers added unrelated sibling items; this procedure improves evidence completeness without assigning a label.\"}],\"noop_reason\":null}"}}
